messages=[TextMessage(id='dae464ac-1a6f-4b61-b226-e6740b78fa33', source='user', models_usage=None, metadata={}, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 8, 10, 48, 20, 791385, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), content='You are helpful user explain bollywood dance', type='TextMessage'), TextMessage(id='4fac23dd-54b4-4481-9c55-f15fded59693', source='agent1', models_usage=RequestUsage(prompt_tokens=18, completion_tokens=698), metadata={}, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 8, 10, 48, 25, 301684, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), content='Welcome to the vibrant world of Bollywood dance! I am so excited to be your instructor. \n\nThink of Bollywood dance not just as one style, but as a **beautiful, energetic fusion.** It’s a mix of classical Indian dance (like Kathak or Bharatanatyam), folk dances (like Bhangra), and modern Western styles (like Hip-Hop, Jazz, and Latin). \n\nIt is all about **storytelling, expression, and pure joy.** Here is a breakdown to get you started:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Essence: "Expression" (Abhinaya)\nIn Bollywood, your face is just as important as your feet. We call this *Abhinaya*.\n*   **The Eyes:** You want to be expressive—smile with your eyes, look surprised, or look playful.\n*   **The Energy:** It’s big, bold, and theatrical. You aren\'t just doing steps; you are performing for an audience.\n\n### 2. The Key Elements\n*   **Graceful Hand Gestures (Mudras):** We use our hands to "tell" the lyrics. If the song says "flower," we might form a flower with our fingers.\n*   **Shoulder Shimmies:** A staple in almost every Bollywood routine. Keep your chest up and shake those shoulders to the beat!\n*   **The "Head Tilt":** A signature Indian movement where you tilt your head slightly side-to-side (it’s more subtle than it looks!).\n*   **Footwork:** Many steps involve rhythmic stomping (Bhangra style) or elegant spins (Classical style).\n\n### 3. The "Bollywood Vibe"\nBollywood dance is usually categorized into a few "moods":\n*   **The Party Track:** High energy, lots of jumping, Bhangra beats, and arm movements.\n*   **The Romantic Number:** Soft, fluid arm movements, lots of twirls, and "soft" footwork.\n*   **The Classical/Semi-Classical:** Focuses on posture, precise hand mudras, and elegant storytelling.\n\n---\n\n### Your First Lesson: The "Shoulder Pop & Step"\nLet’s try a simple move to get your groove going:\n\n1.  **Stance:** Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, knees slightly bent (always keep a "soft" knee so you don\'t hurt yourself).\n2.  **The Arm:** Bring your right arm up in front of you, elbow bent, palm facing your face.\n3.  **The Pop:** On the beat, push your right shoulder forward while "popping" your right arm slightly out. \n4.  **The Step:** As you push your shoulder, step your right foot out to the side. \n5.  **Repeat:** Bring it back to center, then do it on the left side. \n\n**Pro-Tip:** Bollywood is all about **attitude.** If you make a mistake, just keep a big smile on your face and keep moving—that is the most "Bollywood" thing you can do!\n\n---\n\n**Would you like me to suggest a beginner-friendly song to practice to, or would you like to focus on a specific style (like learning a Bhangra move or a graceful hand gesture)?**', type='TextMessage')]
